      "why": "pipelined_m registers every m stages, reducing flip-flop count and potentially power_index versus fully pipelined, while still delivering 1 result/cycle to meet 50 MSPS. The same accuracy-determining parameters (n_iter, data_width, angle_guard, frac_guard, rounding) are constrained identically to pipelined since accuracy is family-independent. m is searched 2-4: m=2 halves the register count vs pipelined, m=4 quarters it, but larger m increases combinational depth per stage which may lower Fmax and hurt throughput. This trade-off between register savings and timing is exactly where the power/accuracy Pareto front for this family lives."
