  "rationale": "iterative and unrolled_k produced zero feasible designs (they cannot hit 50 MSPS), so they are excluded. pipelined already dominates the merged front with 22/22 designs, confirming it is the right family for the throughput constraint. The key trade-off is power_index vs accuracy_bits: I narrow n_iter to 12-16 and data_width to 14-18 because these are the parameters that jointly determine whether max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is met. Below these ranges, accuracy fails; above them, power/area grows without accuracy benefit. I split the budget 50/50 between pipelined and pipelined_m: pipelined to refine the known-feasible region and map the accuracy boundary precisely, and pipelined_m to explore whether reduced register density (larger m) yields lower power_index at the same accuracy, which would shift the Pareto front toward the power-minimum corner that the selection rule targets. Keeping angle_guard and frac_guard in full ranges ensures the search can find the minimal guard-bit configurations that still satisfy the error constraint, which is critical for minimizing power."
